---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Insights & News - DecAltra"
  description="Perspectives on credit decision infrastructure, research, and updates from DecAltra."
>
  <div class="insights-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <div class="kicker">Updates from DecAltra</div>
        <h1 id="page-title">Insights &amp; News</h1>
      </section>
      <section aria-label="Insights and news" class="perspective-grid">
        <article class="perspective-tile">
          <div class="tile-top">
            <span class="tag">Lending economics</span><span
              >Perspective</span
            >
          </div>
          <h2>
            <button data-open="perspective">
              Is the cost of providing credit holding back Europe&rsquo;s
              productivity?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <p class="tile-deck">
            Suitable finance needs to reach viable businesses at the right time,
            through lending processes that are rigorous and economically
            sustainable.
          </p>

          <figure class="research-quote card-quote">
            <blockquote>
              &ldquo;Taking steps to lower delivery and monitoring costs would
              be instrumental in improving the economics of SME lending.&rdquo;
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption>
              <a
                href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/what-drives-differences-in-commercial-banks-product-level-returns"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                >Manning et al. · Bank of England · 2026 ↗</a
              >
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="takeaways">
            <h3>Main takeaways</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Financing constraints can hold back business investment and
                growth.
              </li>
              <li>
                Assessment and monitoring costs can make smaller loans less
                attractive to lenders.
              </li>
              <li>
                Better decision infrastructure can make rigorous lending more
                efficient and scalable.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="tile-sources">
            <h3>Selected research informing our perspective</h3>
            <a
              href="https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/financial-stability-publications/fsr/special/html/ecb.fsrart202411_02~4161cc6124.en.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >ECB · Finance and productivity · 2024 ↗</a
            ><a
              href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/what-drives-differences-in-commercial-banks-product-level-returns"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Bank of England · Lending economics · 2026 ↗</a
            ><a
              href="https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/digitalisation-of-financial-services-access-to-finance-and-aggregate-economic-performance_10c7e583-en.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >OECD · Digitalisation and productivity · 2024 ↗</a
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tile-bottom">
            <button class="note-button" data-open="perspective">
              Read perspective ↗</button
            ><span>DecAltra perspective</span>
          </div>
        </article>


      </section>
      <section class="manifesto">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker">From perspective to practice</div>
          <h2>Better decisions start<br />with better foundations.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            DecAltra connects information, analysis, and professional judgement.
            Our ambition is to help financial institutions spend less time
            preparing a case and more time understanding the opportunity in
            front of them.
          </p>
          <a class="textlink" href="/credit-decisioning"
            >Explore Credit Decisioning <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </section>
    </div><dialog id="perspective" aria-labelledby="perspective-title">
      <div class="dialog-bar">
        <span>DecAltra perspective · Lending economics</span><button
          class="close"
          aria-label="Close perspective">×</button
        >
      </div>
      <article class="article">
        <h2 id="perspective-title">
          Is the cost of providing credit holding back Europe&rsquo;s productivity?
        </h2>
        <p class="small"><strong>By Michael Bolle, Co-founder and CEO, DecAltra</strong></p>
        <p>
          Europe does not lack ambition for greater investment, innovation and
          productivity. My view is that it should also pay closer attention to
          the practical economics of lending: whether viable businesses can
          obtain suitable finance at the right time, through processes that are
          rigorous and sustainable for lenders to operate.
        </p>
        <h3>Finance that fits the opportunity</h3>
        <p>
          The <a href="https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/financial-stability-publications/fsr/special/html/ecb.fsrart202411_02~4161cc6124.en.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">European Central Bank&rsquo;s work on finance and productivity</a>
          makes the case plainly: the way external funding is allocated can
          affect which firms grow, enter and exit a market. When productive
          businesses cannot secure finance, productive capacity can suffer. A
          <a href="https://www.eib.org/en/publications/2024090358-economics-working-paper-2024-08" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2024 European Investment Bank study</a>
          finds that funding difficulties affect firms&rsquo; investment, performance
          and growth, with micro and small businesses and leading innovators
          particularly vulnerable when financing conditions deteriorate.
        </p>
        <p>
          The implication is not that every business should receive a loan.
          Bank credit, private credit and equity each have different roles. The
          task is to match the finance to the opportunity, while maintaining
          sound assessment and oversight.
        </p>
        <h3>The cost of making a decision</h3>
        <p>
          For financial institutions, the cost of assessing, documenting and
          monitoring a loan to a small business can be high relative to the size
          of that loan. Lending economics shape where financial institutions can
          profitably devote attention and capacity. When the cost of
          understanding a business is too high, a viable opportunity may take
          longer to finance, receive less suitable funding, or not be pursued at
          all.
        </p>
        <figure class="research-quote">
          <blockquote>
            &ldquo;Taking steps to lower delivery and monitoring costs would be
            instrumental in improving the economics of SME lending. SME loans
            are typically smaller, more heterogeneous and more labour‑intensive
            to assess, which raises operating costs per‑loan and depresses
            returns. Investment in digitalisation, automation and data‑driven
            credit processes can materially reduce these costs by streamlining
            underwriting, improving risk assessment, and enabling more efficient
            ongoing monitoring.&rdquo;
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            Manning, Babu, Bourdais &amp; Włodarski · Bank of England · 19 June
            2026<br /><a
              href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/what-drives-differences-in-commercial-banks-product-level-returns"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >What drives differences in commercial banks&#8217; product level
              returns? ↗</a
            >
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>
          The Bank’s
          <a
            href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/what-drives-differences-in-commercial-banks-product-level-returns"
            >analysis of lending returns</a
          >
          identifies higher impairment rates and operating costs as the main
          contributors to lower estimated SME lending profitability. Its
          estimates depend on cost-allocation assumptions and do not describe
          every bank’s experience.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is not an argument for lower lending standards. It is an argument
          for making the work needed to meet those standards more efficient,
          connected and repeatable. Underwriting, compliance, monitoring and
          servicing involve substantial work per borrower. A smaller company may
          borrow less than a large corporate but still require a robust
          assessment, a clear audit trail and continuing oversight.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <a href="https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/digitalisation-of-financial-services-access-to-finance-and-aggregate-economic-performance_10c7e583-en.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OECD finds</a>
          that financial-sector digitalisation is associated with stronger
          average industry productivity growth, with larger effects in
          intangible-intensive sectors. Its cross-country estimates show an
          association, not proof that digitalisation alone causes growth. But
          they reinforce the case for reducing avoidable information and process
          frictions in the provision of finance.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://www.bancaditalia.it/pubblicazioni/temi-discussione/2023/2023-1406/index.html?com.dotmarketing.htmlpage.language=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Banca d&#8217;Italia&rsquo;s study of lending during the pandemic</a>
          found that more digitalised banks expanded credit more, particularly
          to smaller, financially sounder firms. Its crisis-period setting means
          the findings should not be read as a universal rule. But they support
          a practical proposition: better information flows and digital
          processes can increase a lender&rsquo;s capacity to assess and serve
          businesses.
        </p>
        <p>
          Technology alone cannot resolve every financing gap. It cannot make an
          unsuitable loan suitable, remove uncertainty from an early-stage
          business, or replace professional judgement. Its proper role is to
          reduce repeated preparation, connect evidence to analysis, and give
          experienced professionals more time to understand the opportunity in
          front of them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Here is an anecdotal observation from DecAltra&rsquo;s experience working
          with clients, rather than a general empirical finding. Creating a
          credit memorandum can take weeks. The work is not only the analysis
          itself. It is also gathering information from separate systems,
          checking figures, explaining adjustments and assembling a decision
          record that colleagues can review.
        </p>
        <p>
          The cost continues after approval when a decision cannot be retraced
          easily. If the source information, assumptions and professional
          judgement behind a credit decision are dispersed, a team has to
          reconstruct its understanding when it monitors a borrower, prepares a
          renewal or investigates a change in performance.
        </p>
        <p>
          In our experience, this makes it harder for an institution to build on
          the intelligence created by earlier decisions. The question is not
          only how quickly a case can be prepared, but whether the understanding
          created in that work can be carried forward.
        </p>
        <h3>A practical productivity question</h3>
        <p>
          If Europe wants more productive investment, it should ask whether the
          operational cost of delivering credit is preventing capable lenders
          from serving viable businesses at scale. The <a href="https://www.eib.org/files/publications/20240354_investment_report_2024_en.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">EIB&rsquo;s work on investment and productivity</a>
          suggests that deeper, better-integrated finance can improve the
          allocation of capital towards productive firms; this is a long-term
          relationship, not a guarantee from any individual loan.
        </p>
        <p>
          The practical objective is better allocation of suitable finance,
          enabled by reliable information, efficient analysis, transparent
          evidence and informed professional judgement. Technology can expand
          capacity, but it cannot make an unsuitable loan suitable or replace
          professional judgement.
        </p>
        <blockquote>
          Improving the economics of rigorous lending could help viable
          businesses access suitable finance sooner, supporting investment and
          productivity without compromising credit standards.
        </blockquote>
        <p class="small editorial-note">
          Written by DecAltra. This is an interpretation of the research cited
          below; it does not represent the views of the cited institutions.
        </p>
        <h3>Research references</h3>
        <ol class="references">
          <li>
            European Central Bank.
            <a
              href="https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/financial-stability-publications/fsr/special/html/ecb.fsrart202411_02~4161cc6124.en.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Low firm productivity: the role of finance and the implications
              for financial stability.</a
            > Financial Stability Review, November 2024.
          </li>
          <li>
            European Investment Bank.
            <a
              href="https://www.eib.org/en/publications/2024090358-economics-working-paper-2024-08"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Do financing conditions pose a threat to the performance and
              transformation of SMEs?</a
            > Economics Working Paper 2024/08.
          </li>
          <li>
            European Investment Bank.
            <a
              href="https://www.eib.org/files/publications/20240354_investment_report_2024_en.pdf"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Investment Report 2024/2025: Innovation, integration and
              simplification in Europe.</a
            > 2025.
          </li>
          <li>
            OECD.
            <a
              href="https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/digitalisation-of-financial-services-access-to-finance-and-aggregate-economic-performance_10c7e583-en.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Digitalisation of financial services, access to finance and
              aggregate economic performance.</a
            > OECD Working Paper, 2024.
          </li>
          <li>
            Colm Manning, Prashant Babu, Ben Bourdais and Robert Włodarski.
            <a
              href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/what-drives-differences-in-commercial-banks-product-level-returns"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >What drives differences in commercial banks&#8217; product level
              returns?</a
            >
            Bank of England, Bank Insights, 19 June 2026.
          </li>
          <li>
            Sarah Breeden and Colm Manning.
            <a
              href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/finance-growth-and-productive-investment-what-is-the-fpc-assessing-in-2026"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Finance, growth and productive investment: what is the FPC
              assessing in 2026?</a
            >
            Bank of England, Bank Insights, 22 September 2026.
          </li>
          <li>
            Bank of England.
            <a
              href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-overground/2025/unlocking-growth-what-can-the-literature-tell-us-about-whats-holding-back-high-growth-firms"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Unlocking growth: what can the literature tell us about
              what&#8217;s holding back high-growth firms?</a
            >
            Bank Overground, 2 October 2025. Prepared with the help of Sudipto Karmakar
            and Isabelle Roland.
          </li>
          <li>
            Nicola Branzoli, Edoardo Rainone and Ilaria Supino.
            <a
              href="https://www.bancaditalia.it/pubblicazioni/temi-discussione/2023/2023-1406/index.html?com.dotmarketing.htmlpage.language=1"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >The role of banks&#8217; technology adoption in credit markets
              during the pandemic.</a
            >
            Banca d&#8217;Italia, Working Paper 1406, March 2023.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </article>
    </dialog>

  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  const root = document.querySelector('.insights-page');
  root?.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-open]').forEach(button => {
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const dialog = root.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>(
        '#' + button.dataset.open
      );
      dialog?.showModal();
    });
  });
  root?.querySelectorAll<HTMLDialogElement>('dialog').forEach(dialog => {
    dialog
      .querySelector('.close')
      ?.addEventListener('click', () => dialog.close());
    dialog.addEventListener('click', event => {
      if (event.target !== dialog) return;
      const rect = dialog.getBoundingClientRect();
      if (
        event.clientX < rect.left ||
        event.clientX > rect.right ||
        event.clientY < rect.top ||
        event.clientY > rect.bottom
      )
        dialog.close();
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .insights-page {
    --ink: #17201d;
    --muted: #626f69;
    --line: #d8e0db;
    --green: #496d58;
    --display: 'Mona Sans', sans-serif;
    color: var(--ink);
    font:
      15px/1.65 Inter,
      sans-serif;
  }
  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  button {
    font: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  a:focus-visible,
  button:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid #629478;
    outline-offset: 5px;
  }
  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .wrap {
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin: auto;
    padding: 0 40px;
  }
  .intro {
    padding: 57px 0 39px;
  }
  .kicker {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 28px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-mist-700);
  }
  .kicker::before {
    content: '';
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.6vw, 60px);
    margin: 17px 0 20px;
  }
  .perspective-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 26px;
    margin-top: 44px;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .perspective-tile {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: subgrid;
    grid-row: span 7;
    row-gap: 0;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 34px;
    transition:
      box-shadow 0.2s,
      border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .perspective-tile:hover {
    border-color: #9aad9b;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 30px #243a2e0b;
  }
  .tile-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    color: var(--color-mist-700);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 24px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .tag {
    color: #52725d;
    background: #edf3ed;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .perspective-tile h2 {
    font-size: 34px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 26px 0 18px;
  }
  .perspective-tile h2 button {
    text-align: left;
    font: inherit;
    letter-spacing: inherit;
    color: inherit;
    padding: 0;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
  }
  .perspective-tile h2 button::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  .tile-deck {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .research-quote {
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    padding: 24px;
    background: #203d30;
    color: #fff;
    border-radius: 9px;
  }
  .research-quote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    font: 500 21px/1.4 var(--display);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .research-quote figcaption {
    font-size: 10px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #d6e1d6;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .research-quote a {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .card-quote {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    min-height: 210px;
  }
  .takeaways {
    background: #f1f5ef;
    border-radius: 9px;
    padding: 22px;
    margin: 10px 0 28px;
  }
  .perspective-tile h3 {
    font:
      600 11px/1.5 Inter,
      sans-serif;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .takeaways ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    list-style: disc;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #40574a;
  }
  .takeaways li + li {
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  .tile-sources {
    padding-bottom: 26px;
  }
  .tile-sources a {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 8px 0;
    color: #486652;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .tile-bottom {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 20px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .note-button {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 550;
  }
  .note-button:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .tile-bottom button {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .tile-bottom > span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 10px;
  }
  .manifesto {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
    gap: 60px;
    padding: 43px 0;
    margin: 62px 0 30px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .manifesto h2 {
    font-size: 28px;
    margin-top: 13px;
  }
  .manifesto p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }
  .manifesto a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: #171b1d;
  }
  .manifesto a span {
    margin-left: 6px;
    font-size: 19px;
    color: #0a7e7d;
  }
  .textlink:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  dialog {
    margin: auto;
    width: min(780px, calc(100% - 32px));
    max-height: 88vh;
    overflow: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 17px;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: #fafbf9;
  }
  dialog::backdrop {
    background: #10201899;
    backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
  }
  .dialog-bar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    background: #fafbf9;
    padding: 18px 28px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .dialog-bar span {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--green);
  }
  .close {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: white;
    width: 35px;
    height: 35px;
    font-size: 21px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .article {
    padding: 34px 45px 44px;
  }
  .article h2 {
    font-size: 38px;
    margin-bottom: 23px;
  }
  .article h3 {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin: 28px 0 12px;
  }
  .article p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: #5d6d62;
    margin: 0 0 15px;
  }
  .article a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .article blockquote {
    margin: 25px 0;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    border-left: 3px solid #a6bca2;
    background: #edf2e9;
    font: 500 24px/1.5 var(--display);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: #37513c;
  }
  .article .research-quote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .article ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 22px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .references {
    list-style: decimal;
    padding-left: 20px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .references li + li {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .editorial-note {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }
  .article .small {
